 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Pick the spot in the clearest spot in the open air as high up as possible. Avoid any trees or shrubs that lose their leaves. That's often the most popular spot. Just make sure there's nothing rotten or low under there. That's often the root system pushing up through the soil. Pull the branches off and spread the leaves out under them. Avoid the area directly around the fire, and don't use it as seat. The ground gets hot and can burn your bottom. Exactly. And try to keep the tent as flat as you can, so there's no spot for a drop of rain to pool up.",
